 you know  um  like fun new ideas and things like that  that were really exciting but  they also captured i think simon's voice  really well but also made it a little  bit their own  um and so it was kind of it's always  exciting when there's  sort of new energy i think  well and it was also unique for a lot of  people i i  assume because i think it was for a lot  of people it was their first project  backed  after the pandemic what was it like to  be back on a set during that  you know bizarre we were like  it's we were shooting in um  on this ranch in california in kind of  like a big spike of covert in california  um so that was pretty  freaky and um but luckily we were  shooting  i mean completely outside luckily the  oregon trail is  we're outdoors and um can stay pretty  like distanced and stuff so i think we  felt  like it was the safest possible way to  to be working  right now um but  also very strange of course yeah it's  really like  i was personally just like so happy to  have like somewhere to go  like i'm losing my mind but so it was  really like it was really nice to be  with people again  but one of the joys of making especially  a show that's like a few months is  getting to know the crew  and it's always so awkward and hard with  this covet part of it all  because like every you don't even get to  really interact with people that much  but on this show they did something cool  where  everyone had a name card uh badge  that had their face on it a picture of  their face  so at least you could somewhat be like  oh i might  recognize this person if i ever saw them  at starbucks  after they shoot um so it made it a  little bit more human which i was like  yeah we should do that on everything um  but yeah  well i'm sure for both of you who are  probably itching to get back to work and  get back to acting and then i'm sure  it's just really strange where you  feel like no one wants to come near you  while you're on set  yeah yeah and it definitely started  where like  you know we as actors in the beginning  were like yeah you know even we'll keep  distance from each other but then we  were like a month or two and we're like  lunch in your trailer lunch and mine  you're just like  i guess if we're taking our masks off  and we're tested like at least can we  hang out with each other because we're  so starved for like connection  we started to play a fun game of guess  that mouse  where we kind of like yeah it's really  bizarre not seeing  someone's mouth and it's shocking every  time because we'll see them like take it  off at like the lunch tent  or something or having water in between  takes and it's like  yeah a complete shock every time it's  never the mouth you think it's gonna be  so um that that brought something fun  and new to that  was also curious that i mean obviously  each season is changing setting and  characters  how much input do you guys have in the  creation of the characters that you're  you're going to be playing in the  upcoming season  uh zero  you didn't get to pick out your cool  bounty hunter outfit no  i always feel like at least i'll speak  for myself i'm like find out right  before we're about to go table and i'm  like what  is happening yeah the second season i  got to go to the writer's room so that  so i did get to i guess do that once uh  and then this season they did invite us  to do that but it was on zoom and  i'm not trying to add more zoom time to  my  existence on this planet so i was like  i'll keep it as a surprise but um  but yeah we they always ask and then we  say  stuff and then sometimes it makes it in  but it's kind of like a roll of the dice  in a very fun way where i'm like  you're opening a present and you're like  what am i gonna get to do yeah  did you guys watch any i mean i've only  been able to see one episode but it's  clearly kind of playing on a bunch of  western tropes  did you guys watch any westerns in  preparation of of  doing the season i started watching  bonanza  with my mom because she grew up watching  that and she loves that  and yeah you know and i also it's like  i love the horses um and then i also  watched  searches um which i really  i really enjoy but then it also stresses  me out because then you see the horses  go down  like they'll be shooting and and then  i'm like this is actually  i just want the horses to be to be happy  and  free and galloping but um  i love westerns i feel like it's it it's  such a it's such a dream to like get to  actually be in that fantasy land  it's really it's such a fun genre i  can't stand westerns  [Laughter]  i find them so boring but i will say i  have a new respect for them now  because i'm like god this is hard like  it's making one thing that was  fun we our dp blake mcclure  who's incredible he shot it like it was  a western so we had these  really huge like lights that were  actually  fire i think it was really and  yeah like yeah on like a bright day he  would put a huge  sunlight in front of our faces so we  were like and we were squinting  and we like we kept being like that's  exactly my eye line like i can't  like hey like you know cleanings would  that's why he's squinting like  yeah you always just look like the sun  is in front of your face  that acting style is really informed by  how you can't  open your eyes and and see if that makes  sense  there did seem to be some bright  lighting on there um my final question  for you both  should there be a season four do you  have an ideal hopeful scenario or  setting that you would  get to tackle that one tackle on that  one  mine is dogs i just came up with this  this morning because i knew i'd be asked  just like  a season with dogs doesn't that sound  fun  we're dog walkers just go really like  micro  yeah well that gets very meta with like  daniel's dog walking  meeting oh right train wreck  that's kind of cool if we could kind of  expand on that meme  it's like the golden age of content  we're expanding on daniel and i mean  three years ago for ten episodes for us  i wanna go to space i wanna go to the  future i want  like aliens i want that  i'm into it uh well thank you guys both  so much  i love the show i think you guys are  both fantastic in it and i can't wait to  see the rest of the season  thank you

